WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.880
Spatial transcriptomics reveals how neighboring tissues send WNT and BMP signals that steer early gonadal cell fate in human embryos. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 230. Prime editing in major crops comes next, then a global wildlife trade census, then field trials that held yields through drought and flood. Researchers at the Institute of Zoology of the Chinese Academy of Sciences mapped male and female human embryos at Carnegie Stages 15, 19, and 23.

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:33.540
in work published in science and reported by Fizz.org.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.900
They combine stereosec spatial transcriptomics

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:40.280
with single cell multiomics, tissue protein imaging,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.540
and human embryonic stem cell models.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.160
Stereosec profiling resolved major gonadol,

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.500
adrenal cortical, renal, mesenchymal, and neural populations,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.980
and classified the data set into 33 cell types.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.980
At stage 15, the gonadol primordium receives those signals

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.100
from the adjacent mesonephros and adrenal primordium.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:08.160
Treating human embryonic stem cell derived intermediate mesoderm with BMP-7, N-C-A-M-1,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:15.560
and CHIR-99021 increased early gonadal marker expression and shifted transcriptomes toward

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.620
the in vivo early gonadal state.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.420
Later stages showed Pax-8 expressing retay cells more similar to mesonephric mesenchym, than

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:30.220
to gonadol somatic cells, and computational perturbation plus in vitro Pax-8 knockdown

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.860
indicated that Pax-8 helps maintain retail cell identity.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:39.340
Three transcriptionally distinct steroidogenic populations appeared in the first trimester,

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.160
with fetal laidig cells in the male gonad and two adrenal fetal zone states.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:51.240
Fetal zone state 2 expressed SCARB-1, LDLR, and cortisol synthesis genes, while fetal

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.640
Zone State 1 showed stronger de novo cholesterol synthesis marked by SRE-BF2.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:02.080
That spatial work supplies a native context map of how mesonephoric and adrenal cues

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:09.680
shape gonadal primordium fate, and the stem cell tests turn WNT, BMP, and NCAM into inputs

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.140
for directed differentiation aimed at functional gonadal tissue.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.780
The retail cell data raised the possibility that a subset of gonadal supporting cells arises

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:23.680
through a mesonephros linked root, rather than solely from the gonadol somatic lineage.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.860
If that root proves reproducible in culture, it could expand the cell sources available

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:33.400
for regenerative approaches to disorders of sex development or fertility preservation.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.380
One immediate experimental step is to test whether targeted modulation of the three-factor cocktail

00:02:39.380 --> 00:02:43.880
improves yield or stability of induced gonadol cells in longer-term cultures.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:49.140
The steroidogenic data further indicate that adrenal gonad coordination of cholesterol

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:54.380
utilization and cortisol synthesis begins in the first trimester, including in programs

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:57.120
that can diverge between male and female embryos.

00:02:57.882 --> 00:03:02.842
The smart PE system, built at the Institute of Genetics and Developmental Biology of the

00:03:02.842 --> 00:03:08.302
Chinese Academy of Sciences, raised prime editing efficiency in dichot crops, according

00:03:08.302 --> 00:03:09.802
to a study in nature plants.

00:03:09.802 --> 00:03:15.122
events. Inserting the start cis-regulatory element upstream of cast 9 raised transcript

00:03:15.122 --> 00:03:22.262
levels 2.1 fold and lifted editing efficiency at 4 Arabidopsis targets by about 1.8 fold.

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:27.922
Complementary mismatched bases in the reverse transcriptase templates of dual peg RNAs then

00:03:27.922 --> 00:03:33.842
lifted average editing activity more than 6 fold to roughly 10% at those 4 Arabidopsis

00:03:33.842 --> 00:03:39.782
targets. Continuous mismatches or mismatches spaced 3 base pairs apart yielded the

00:03:39.782 --> 00:03:45.582
highest efficiencies reaching 20% while intervals of six base pairs are more sharply reduced

00:03:45.582 --> 00:03:46.242
performance.

00:03:46.862 --> 00:03:51.082
In tomato proto-plasts, six of nine targets exceeded 10% efficiency.

00:03:51.702 --> 00:03:57.582
In soybean, nine of 11 targets exceeded 5%, and five rapeseed targets reached or exceeded

00:03:57.582 --> 00:03:58.862
about 10%.

00:03:58.862 --> 00:04:04.602
Using synonymous substitutions to create reverse transcriptase template mismatches, the team

00:04:04.602 --> 00:04:10.362
Some generated single amino acid substitutions in soybean and tomato at efficiencies 1.6 to

00:04:10.362 --> 00:04:13.282
11.1 times higher than standard prime editing.

00:04:13.822 --> 00:04:19.402
Stable transformation produced homozygous edits at the SLOR2 locus in tomato hairy roots

00:04:19.402 --> 00:04:21.082
at 7.3%.

00:04:21.082 --> 00:04:25.722
Versus only 1.0% heterozygous edits with standard prime editing.

00:04:26.282 --> 00:04:30.162
And seamless flag tag insertions reached up to 32% efficiency.

00:04:30.162 --> 00:04:36.548
University of Melbourne researchers integrated cross-sectoral trade monitoring data and estimated

00:04:36.548 --> 00:04:44.048
at least 107,356 species are used in traded worldwide in an analysis published in science

00:04:44.048 --> 00:04:44.688
advances.

00:04:45.188 --> 00:04:49.648
That figure more than doubles the previous estimate of approximately 50,000 species.

00:04:50.308 --> 00:04:53.828
Legal trade is worth roughly 10 times the value of illegal trade.

00:04:54.288 --> 00:04:59.208
Only the United States systematically records and publicly shares trade data across wide

00:04:59.208 --> 00:05:03.708
taxonomic ranges, and equivalent records are absent for most other countries.

00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:09.545
Something most people get wrong is that wildlife trade is a narrow illegal market in elephants,

00:05:09.905 --> 00:05:15.505
tigers, or pangolins, when the pooled records run across plants, animals, and fungi in both

00:05:15.505 --> 00:05:16.945
legal and illegal channels.

00:05:17.485 --> 00:05:23.605
For some groups, 75% of traded species appear solely in United States data sets, leaving

00:05:23.605 --> 00:05:26.125
the remaining trade invisible to global assessments.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:31.705
The absence of quantity, origin, and population data for the great majority of these species

00:05:31.705 --> 00:05:36.085
prevents any reliable judgment of whether current harvest levels threaten survival.

00:05:36.785 --> 00:05:42.125
Because legal commerce already outstrips illegal commerce in economic value, the scale of

00:05:42.125 --> 00:05:46.245
pressure on biodiversity is larger than enforcement statistics alone suggest.

00:05:47.025 --> 00:05:51.765
Improved customs and zooo-sanitary recording systems could close the largest gaps without

00:05:51.765 --> 00:05:57.725
new infrastructure, yet no coordinated international effort currently exists to standardize those records.

00:05:58.305 --> 00:06:03.245
The global biodiversity framework target on trade accounts for only around two or three percent

00:06:03.245 --> 00:06:09.925
of species in trade, and misses the other 97 percent. Repurposing existing customs processes could

00:06:09.925 --> 00:06:16.105
create a monitoring system, but that requires further engagement to implement at scale. Until such data

00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:20.885
to exist, risk assessments and sustainability claims rest on an incomplete foundation.

00:06:21.345 --> 00:06:27.305
Even as legal trade in timber, seafood, medicinal plants, pets, cut flowers, ornamental fish,

00:06:27.685 --> 00:06:32.065
and fungi already operates at a volume most monitoring systems do not capture.

00:06:33.051 --> 00:06:37.631
Researchers from the Center for Carbon Research in Tropical Agriculture at the University of

00:06:37.631 --> 00:06:44.351
Sao Paulo tested varied crop rotations with continuous soil cover in Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil.

00:06:44.351 --> 00:06:49.631
The approach reduced damage from both droughts and floods while raising overall productivity.

00:06:50.151 --> 00:06:54.731
Continuous vegetation cover and rotation diversity were the two practices that delivered

00:06:54.731 --> 00:06:55.791
the measured protection.

00:06:56.803 --> 00:07:02.503
FIU biologist Alessandro Catanazi and colleagues formally named for previously undocumented

00:07:02.503 --> 00:07:04.303
frog species collected in Peru.

00:07:04.983 --> 00:07:08.823
The descriptions add concrete records to the country's amphibian inventory.

00:07:09.643 --> 00:07:14.503
Verified species identities are what future ecological and conservation assessments require.

00:07:14.503 --> 00:07:20.252
A University of Massachusetts Amherst team measured erosion rates across mountain landscapes

00:07:20.252 --> 00:07:25.292
and found weaker rock erodes three times faster than harder rock even on gentler slopes.

00:07:25.872 --> 00:07:30.592
The finding revises models that link erosion rates to carbon dioxide release from rock

00:07:30.592 --> 00:07:31.132
weathering.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:36.170
A study measured significantly higher blood levels of Preston in people with chronic

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:40.290
tenitis compared with controls, as reported via science subreddit.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.970
Preston is a protein expressed in cochlear outer hair cells.

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:50.910
The protein is proposed as a candidate circulating biomarker, though the author's note further validation is required.

00:07:51.894 --> 00:08:00.394
Late-life administration of a three-component senolytic vaccine lowered senescence markers in female B6 mice, according to lifespan.io.

00:08:00.614 --> 00:08:05.234
The treatment produced a 12% increase in median lifespan in those female animals.

00:08:05.874 --> 00:08:10.094
Short-lived control groups complicate direct interpretation of the longevity effect.

00:08:10.094 --> 00:08:16.291
In brief, a psychological bias may be keeping United States drug laws out of step with scientific

00:08:16.291 --> 00:08:21.431
evidence, helping explain why those policies often fail to reflect what research actually

00:08:21.431 --> 00:08:21.851
shows.

00:08:22.391 --> 00:08:27.411
A tiny glass chip from Harriott-Watt University has linked two telescopes so they act as a single

00:08:27.411 --> 00:08:28.491
powerful instrument.

00:08:29.011 --> 00:08:40.491
Before we go, circulating Preston still needs that further validation before it can stand as a

